<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Central Rada</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1917">1917</a>–<a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Central Council of Ukraine</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/radaa">Rada</a> was the Ukrainian revolutionary council formed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kyiv</a> in March 1917 under the historian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mykhailo-hrushevsky">Mykhailo Hrushevsky</a>. Through its Universals it proclaimed Ukrainian autonomy, then the Ukrainian People's Republic, and full independence in January 1918. It signed a separate peace with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-powers">Central Powers</a>, who dissolved it in April 1918 in favour of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pavlo-skoropadsky">Pavlo Skoropadsky</a>'s Hetmanate.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/central-rada.jpg" alt="Central Rada" width="320" height="365" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alex Tora · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_Arms_of_UNR.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
